WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.850
This exercise adds a short synthetic DNA
record to a new Entry.

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.480
In the sidebar, click New entry.

3
00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:11.400
Type FASTA practice in the name field and
press Enter.

4
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:15.640
Click Paste a sequence and paste the
complete example from the guide.

5
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:18.680
Include the first line beginning with a
greater-than sign.

6
00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:23.320
That line supplies the name; the four
sequence lines supply eighty bases.

7
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.280
Check the preview before submitting.

8
00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:28.040
It says FASTA and eighty base pairs.

9
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.360
The upward-arrow button now says Add FASTA,
eighty base pairs.

10
00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:36.840
Click it once. The new block is named SEAL
beginner practice.

11
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.200
Its header identifies DNA and eighty base
pairs.

12
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.400
Select the block and open Overview in the
Inspector.

13
00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:45.730
Check the same name and length there.

14
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.680
The example has no ambiguous bases and no
feature annotations.

15
00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:53.802
If your length differs, compare your input
with the guide before continuing.
